13. Huckleberry must comply with all applicable orders, directions and conditions, and obtain and must 
comply with all applicable tenures, licences, regulations, approvals, standards and permits, or other 
authorities, which may include or result from, but are not necessarily limited to, the following:
(a) Commercial Transport Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 55, for licencing of commercial vehicles;
(b) Environment Management Act, S.B.C. 1981, c. 14, for an impact assessment and/or 
environmental protection order;
(c) Fire Services Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 133, for the storage, use and handling of 
flammable and combustible liquids;
(d) Fisheries Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 137, for a licence to collect fish samples;
(e) Forest Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 140, and Forest Practice Code Act, S.B.C. 1994, c. 41 for 
a licence to cut and remove merchantable timber on Crown Land, and approval for access 
road development;
(f) Gas Safety Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 149, for installation or alteration of gas piping;
(g) Health Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 161, for sewage disposal permits, for food and for the 
operation and abandonment of industrial camps;
(h) Heritage Conservation Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 165, to alter a provincial heritage or 
archaeological site;
(i) Highway Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 167, for joining industrial roads to public highways;
(j) Land Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 214, for disturbances or use of Crown land;
(k) Mineral Tenure Act, S.B.C. 1988, c. 5, for the acquisition of claims and leases; 
(l) Mines Act, S.B.C. 1989, c. 56, and the Health, Safety and Reclamation Code, for a 
program for the protection and reclamation of the land and water courses affected by a 
mine, as well as mine plans, worker health and safety and mechanical and/or electrical 
requirements;
(m) Mining Right of Way Act, S.B.C. 1989, c. 57, for the acquisition of rights of way or the 
use of existing roads;
(n) Motor Vehicle Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 288, for use of public roads;
(o) Municipal Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 290, for conformity to municipal and regional by-
laws;
(p) Pesticide Control Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 322, for a permit to use pesticides;
(q) Pipeline Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 328, for approval of high pressure pipelines;
(r) Power Engineers & Boiler & Pressure Vessel Safety Act, S.B.C. 1981, c. 25, for 
approval of boilers, pressure vessels and refrigeration plants;
(s) Railway Act, R.S.B.C. 1979, c. 354, for approval to cross railway lines;
(t) Transport of Dangerous Goods Act, S.B.C. 1985, c. 1
